<!doctype html>
<html lang="{var:content.locale default=`en`}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    {include:`partials/seo-head.html.dtmpl`}
    {slot:head}
    {loop:site.theme.css}
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="{var:item.url}">
    {endloop}
</head>
<body>
    {slot:body}
        {include:`partials/header.html.dtmpl`}
        <main class="container py-4" style="{var:page.contentMaxWidthStyle}">
            {slot:content}{endslot}
        </main>
        {include:`partials/footer.html.dtmpl`}
    {endslot}
    {loop:site.theme.js}
        <script src="{var:item.url}" type="module"></script>
    {endloop}
    {slot:scripts}
    {comment}
      Two widgets that make a PROMISE to a visitor, gated here rather than
      inside their own files -- each of those is one {verbatim} block, where a
      directive prints as text with no error. Defaults are off; see
      Web\Infrastructure\Settings\PublicWidgetsSettingsContributor for why.

      The analytics / experiments / personalization partials are NOT gated on
      consent here: each reads the consent cookie and `data-consent` for itself,
      so with no banner they see no consent and stay off on their own.
    {endcomment}
    {if:site.features.cookieConsent}
      {include:`partials/cookie-consent.html.dtmpl`}
    {endif}
    {include:`partials/analytics.html.dtmpl`}
    {include:`partials/experiments.html.dtmpl`}
    {include:`partials/personalization.html.dtmpl`}
    {if:site.features.chat}
      {include:`partials/dynamic-chat-widget.html.dtmpl`}
    {endif}
</body>
</html>
